## Archive Gzip Codec Slice
##
## Part of the Alya Language package ecosystem (https://github.com/alya-lang).
## TAR.GZ (`*.tar.gz` / `*.tgz`) packing through `compress` codecs for
## compression plus exact-size native decompression (see `gunzip_exact`).

import "./tar.alya"
import "./file.alya"
import "compress" as compress_pkg

## Packs entries into a gzip-compressed tarball image.
##
## ### Parameters
## - `entries`: Array of `ArchiveEntry` structs to store.
##
## ### Returns
## Gzip-compressed tar image as a byte array.
pub function targz_pack(entries) -> array
    return compress_pkg::gzip(tar_build(entries))
end

## Unpacks a gzip-compressed tarball image back into entry records.
##
## Decompression targets the ISIZE-declared exact size, so tarballs of any
## size unpack without output-growth limits. Only single-member gzip
## streams are supported.
##
## ### Parameters
## - `data`: Gzip-compressed tar image byte array.
##
## ### Returns
## Array of `ArchiveEntry` structs, or throws on corrupt input.
pub function targz_unpack(data) -> array
    return tar_parse(gunzip_exact(data))
end
